    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The rest of katakana",
     "texto": [
      "These rows complete the syllabary. The little dashes (゛) and the little circle (゜) work the same as in hiragana: **ハ** ha → **バ** ba → **パ** pa.",
      "Katakana is used to write countries and nationalities: **スペイン** (Spain), **メキシコ** (Mexico), **アメリカ** (United States), **フランス** (France)."
