    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How to write your name",
     "texto": [
      "Your name is adapted to Japanese syllables. As there are no single consonants (except n), a **u** or an **o** is added: Carlos → **カルロス** (karurosu), David → **ダビド** (dabido).",
      "Japanese has no **l**: the r row is used. Laura → **ラウラ** (raura).",
      "Japanese has no **v** either: the b is used. And the sound of the Spanish **j** in «Javier» is written with the h row: Javier → **ハビエル** (habieru)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
